values ('a2b3c4d5-6e7f-4a09-8c99-9d0e1f2a3b09', 'form-and-analysis', 'Form and Analysis', 'This course develops advanced skills in analyzing musical structure across phrase, theme, movement, and multi-movement levels. Students study motives, phrases, periods, cadences, binary and ternary forms, variations, rondos, sonata and concerto forms, fugue, large-scale cycles, 20th-century and contemporary forms, and analytical writing. The course emphasizes score study, listening, formal diagrams, historical style, evidence-based interpretation, and clear written argument.');

